WEBVTT

00:00:08.230 --> 00:00:12.440
This is Murase Youka.
She will be your classmate starting today.

00:00:12.440 --> 00:00:14.240
She's one year older than you guys.

00:00:14.490 --> 00:00:16.780
Mentioning my age wasn't necessary.

00:00:16.780 --> 00:00:17.940
Is that so?

00:00:17.940 --> 00:00:19.870
Anyway, be nice to her.

00:00:20.330 --> 00:00:22.240
Sera, you'll be in charge of her.

00:00:22.240 --> 00:00:22.990
Yes, sir.

00:02:07.190 --> 00:02:08.600
<i>Close your eyes.</i>

00:02:08.600 --> 00:02:12.150
<i>Think of what you deem the purest.</i>

00:02:12.690 --> 00:02:15.690
<i>That is your purity.</i>

00:02:15.690 --> 00:02:19.950
<i>There are plenty of things in
this world that are as pure as that.</i>

00:02:20.160 --> 00:02:22.370
<i>Where are they?</i>

00:02:22.370 --> 00:02:24.120
<i>They're everywhere!</i>

00:02:24.120 --> 00:02:26.580
<i>As long as you have purity within your heart,</i>

00:02:26.580 --> 00:02:28.710
<i>you'll be able to find things
that are just as pure anywhere.</i>

00:02:29.290 --> 00:02:35.130
<i>But it probably isn't smart to live
searching only for pure things.</i>

00:02:37.340 --> 00:02:37.880
Huh?

00:02:56.530 --> 00:02:58.950
A service club at Ashiharabashi High School?

00:02:58.950 --> 00:03:02.370
Yeah. I'll be the club advisor
and you guys will be the members.

00:03:02.370 --> 00:03:04.530
So we're being monitored?

00:03:04.530 --> 00:03:08.160
Don't you two want to help others
with your combined abilities?

00:03:09.910 --> 00:03:11.750
What are you going to do, Haruki?

00:03:12.420 --> 00:03:15.750
I'll follow your lead, Kei.

00:03:20.170 --> 00:03:20.880
Yes?

00:03:22.970 --> 00:03:24.680
Here is my membership application.

00:03:25.010 --> 00:03:26.760
Thanks.

00:03:27.390 --> 00:03:30.020
Still, he sure was in a rush.

00:03:30.020 --> 00:03:33.770
I mean, making us bring the applications
immediately after the entrance ceremony.

00:03:33.770 --> 00:03:36.610
You're going to continue with the
Service Club even in high school?

00:03:36.770 --> 00:03:39.740
Yeah. I have my reasoning for doing so.

00:03:39.740 --> 00:03:44.280
But if I were to give a reason,
it's because it'd be troublesome not to be in it.

00:03:44.490 --> 00:03:49.750
Still, I'm pretty sure there's no reason for you
to be in the Service Club without my ability.

00:03:50.000 --> 00:03:52.080
The same goes for you, too.

00:03:52.080 --> 00:03:56.130
Our abilities don't have any value on their own.

00:03:56.130 --> 00:04:00.170
Besides, if anything, I want to be in the Service Club.

00:04:00.170 --> 00:04:01.760
Why is that?

00:04:01.760 --> 00:04:05.930
When you're in the Service Club, you can gain
access to info regarding special abilities.

00:04:05.930 --> 00:04:08.260
I want to learn more about them.

00:04:08.760 --> 00:04:13.100
But also because I want to get
to know our advisor better.

00:04:13.100 --> 00:04:14.900
You mean, Mr. Tsushima?

00:04:15.150 --> 00:04:19.070
Yeah. I kinda like the guy.

00:04:19.070 --> 00:04:21.280
Don't you wanna join the Service Club?

00:04:21.650 --> 00:04:23.990
I do, as long as I'm there with you.

00:04:27.830 --> 00:04:30.120
Sorry. I made you wait, didn't I?

00:04:30.120 --> 00:04:30.950
Not at all.

00:04:31.620 --> 00:04:33.160
Congrats on your enrollment.

00:04:33.370 --> 00:04:36.880
Thank you. It's good to see you again.

00:04:36.880 --> 00:04:39.880
Everything that comes out
of your mouth sounds sarcastic.

00:04:39.880 --> 00:04:42.260
That hurts. I was being honest.

00:04:44.090 --> 00:04:47.050
Is your name officially written this way?

00:04:47.260 --> 00:04:49.600
Yes, I always write it like that.

00:04:49.600 --> 00:04:50.600
Why?

00:04:50.600 --> 00:04:54.810
My name can be difficult to spell for some people.
It gets messed up pretty often if I don't do it.

00:04:54.810 --> 00:04:56.190
Whatever.

00:04:56.190 --> 00:04:57.520
Anyway, I've accepted these.

00:04:58.060 --> 00:05:01.280
Welcome to the Ashiharabashi
High School Service Club.

00:05:01.280 --> 00:05:03.780
The way you're smiling is kinda sinister, you know.

00:05:03.780 --> 00:05:04.650
I know.

00:05:04.650 --> 00:05:08.990
When I think about it, there's so many
bad things I could do with your abilities.

00:05:09.370 --> 00:05:11.580
So, Mr. Tsushima...

00:05:11.580 --> 00:05:15.250
Why'd you want us to submit our membership
applications right after the entrance ceremony?

00:05:15.500 --> 00:05:17.880
I just wanted to make you guys
club members right away.

00:05:18.080 --> 00:05:20.290
In order to assign us club duties?

00:05:20.290 --> 00:05:20.960
Yeah.

00:05:22.000 --> 00:05:23.670
You guys are best suited for it.

00:05:24.760 --> 00:05:26.970
This happened about two hours ago.

00:05:26.970 --> 00:05:33.310
At around 11:30 a.m, we found a female student
collapsed in front of the school gates.

00:05:33.720 --> 00:05:36.440
That's around the time
the entrance ceremony ended.

00:05:36.440 --> 00:05:37.520
Right.

00:05:37.520 --> 00:05:40.820
A parent found her and immediately
took her to the infirmary.

00:05:41.320 --> 00:05:44.320
She didn't take part in the entrance ceremony.

00:05:44.690 --> 00:05:47.320
This was found on the ground right next to her.

00:05:47.780 --> 00:05:48.820
Take a look at it.

00:05:52.290 --> 00:05:55.870
That's the student who collapsed
in front of the school gates.

00:05:57.040 --> 00:05:59.580
Hello. It's nice to meet you.

00:06:06.800 --> 00:06:09.470
I'm sorry, we're the only ones eating.

00:06:09.470 --> 00:06:12.050
Oh, that's okay! Don't worry about me!

00:06:12.050 --> 00:06:13.810
I've got this instead.

00:06:14.390 --> 00:06:16.810
A strawberry-flavored Candy Candy.

00:06:17.140 --> 00:06:19.310
Do you like Candy Candy?

00:06:19.520 --> 00:06:22.770
Yeah. I've liked sweets for a long time.

00:06:23.230 --> 00:06:27.740
Anyway, is it okay for high schoolers
to stop at a café on their way home?

00:06:27.740 --> 00:06:30.870
It's fine since we're doing this for the Service Club.

00:06:31.070 --> 00:06:32.910
Huh? Really?

00:06:32.910 --> 00:06:33.870
Yes.

00:06:33.870 --> 00:06:37.370
Haruki and I have been in the
Service Club since middle school.

00:06:37.910 --> 00:06:43.170
If it's for the Service Club,
most things count as part of our club activities.

00:06:43.460 --> 00:06:45.880
And if we get a receipt,
the cost is deducted from our club's budget.

00:06:45.880 --> 00:06:47.170
I see.

00:06:48.510 --> 00:06:51.720
Why is she inside a marble?

00:06:51.970 --> 00:06:54.720
She possesses that sort of ability.

00:06:54.720 --> 00:06:59.730
She has the ability to enter the reflected
scenery in things like mirrors or glass shards.

00:07:00.100 --> 00:07:06.230
I guess it's more like she's in the reflection
of the marble rather than inside the marble.

00:07:06.230 --> 00:07:10.110
Her body is asleep on a bed
in the infirmary right now.

00:07:10.910 --> 00:07:13.910
Sera has used her ability twice in the past.

00:07:13.910 --> 00:07:16.790
She's used it at a rate of
about once every two years.

00:07:16.790 --> 00:07:18.000
Is that correct?

00:07:18.000 --> 00:07:20.080
Yeah, probably.

00:07:20.080 --> 00:07:21.120
"Probably"?

00:07:21.120 --> 00:07:23.500
I guess I never really felt it.

00:07:23.920 --> 00:07:25.000
I see.

00:07:25.460 --> 00:07:29.300
<i>Sera Sawako uses her ability without realizing it.</i>

00:07:29.300 --> 00:07:30.970
<i>It isn't done consciously.</i>

00:07:30.970 --> 00:07:34.510
<i>Does that mean there's
a switch deep within her mind?</i>

00:07:34.510 --> 00:07:36.640
Would it be best to reset?

00:07:36.850 --> 00:07:39.770
Well, that's what we were ordered to do.

00:07:40.230 --> 00:07:42.650
I think there's something
else we can do before that.

00:07:42.810 --> 00:07:45.110
What is that something?

00:07:45.110 --> 00:07:48.320
I guess it'd be speaking with Sera first.

00:07:48.650 --> 00:07:50.070
With me?

00:07:50.070 --> 00:07:50.700
Yes.

00:07:51.030 --> 00:07:53.360
There's something I'd like you to tell me about.

00:07:53.360 --> 00:07:55.830
Why did you use your ability?

00:07:56.080 --> 00:07:57.540
"Why"?

00:07:57.540 --> 00:08:01.290
Abilities in Sakurada don't work
unless the user wishes for them to.

00:08:01.620 --> 00:08:05.960
You wished to use your ability at some point in time.

00:08:05.960 --> 00:08:09.300
Before we reset, we'll need to make
certain what your reason was.

00:08:09.300 --> 00:08:12.220
Otherwise, you'll end up in that marble again.

00:08:12.220 --> 00:08:13.800
Um...

00:08:13.800 --> 00:08:16.430
Sorry, I have no idea.

00:08:16.430 --> 00:08:18.310
Before I realized, I was stuck in here.

00:08:18.310 --> 00:08:20.310
It's okay to tell me one thing at a time.

00:08:20.310 --> 00:08:22.560
Can you recall what you did step by step?

00:08:22.560 --> 00:08:27.020
Um, I think I woke up at around 5:30.

00:08:27.230 --> 00:08:29.070
You wake up quite early.

00:08:29.070 --> 00:08:30.860
I've always been like that.

00:08:30.860 --> 00:08:34.410
Whether it's for field trips or sports events,
I'm the kind of person that wakes up early.

00:08:34.700 --> 00:08:36.910
And today it was because
of the entrance ceremony?

00:08:36.910 --> 00:08:38.620
Yeah, probably...

00:08:38.620 --> 00:08:42.250
When I woke up, I changed into my
uniform like usual, ate breakfast...

00:08:44.420 --> 00:08:46.920
Should I tell you what I ate for breakfast, too?

00:08:46.920 --> 00:08:49.170
Yes, please. Just to be safe.

00:08:58.180 --> 00:09:02.350
So, in other words, you were late
because you were looking into the marble?

00:09:02.770 --> 00:09:05.810
I guess it all started when I missed my bus.

00:09:05.810 --> 00:09:08.730
Well, I would've made it in time
even with the next bus.

00:09:08.730 --> 00:09:10.980
But I thought it'd be fine.

00:09:10.980 --> 00:09:14.240
You mean, it'd be fine to be late
for the entrance ceremony?

00:09:14.240 --> 00:09:18.280
I thought skipping out on just
the entrance ceremony would be fine.

00:09:18.280 --> 00:09:23.540
You end up hearing the same old thing
at every ceremony you go to, right?

00:09:23.540 --> 00:09:26.920
It's smarter to wander wherever
you feel, like the shopping district.

00:09:26.920 --> 00:09:30.290
But you still made it to the school gates.

00:09:30.750 --> 00:09:33.670
Yeah. I was pretty half-hearted about it.

00:09:34.420 --> 00:09:40.760
When I was in middle school, I was kind of a
dedicated student, so I'm not used to playing hooky.

00:09:40.760 --> 00:09:45.310
For some reason, I decided to look at the marble
in front of the school gates, and ended up like this.

00:09:45.560 --> 00:09:47.390
Do you like marbles?

00:09:47.390 --> 00:09:50.270
Huh? Yeah, I sort of do.

00:09:50.270 --> 00:09:51.730
What do you like about it?

00:09:53.190 --> 00:09:55.190
Maybe how carefree they are.

00:09:55.190 --> 00:09:55.990
"Carefree"?

00:09:55.990 --> 00:10:00.490
Yeah. The view is squished
and warped, and also inverted.

00:10:00.490 --> 00:10:02.740
It's like they're making fun of the world.

00:10:02.950 --> 00:10:05.370
I don't think they're making fun of it...

00:10:05.370 --> 00:10:09.380
Anyway, I thought that kind
of thing about them was nice.

00:10:16.300 --> 00:10:17.930
Yes? This is Asai.

00:10:17.930 --> 00:10:19.840
Why haven't you reset yet?

00:10:20.140 --> 00:10:23.930
Haruki saved around noon two days ago.

00:10:23.930 --> 00:10:26.770
We can still reset up until noon tomorrow.

00:10:26.770 --> 00:10:31.730
Your duty is just to reset and report
what happened in the past.

00:10:32.230 --> 00:10:34.110
Yes, I'm aware of that.

00:10:34.110 --> 00:10:36.990
Why aren't you resetting immediately, then?

00:10:37.190 --> 00:10:40.610
Well, I want to thoroughly
understand Sera beforehand.

00:10:40.610 --> 00:10:45.490
I want to understand her problems
to learn why she used her ability.

00:10:45.700 --> 00:10:47.710
What are you going to do with that information?

00:10:47.710 --> 00:10:50.790
I'm going to resolve her problems with
a method that's appropriate for her.

00:10:50.790 --> 00:10:53.670
I'll do everything according to your intentions.

00:10:54.090 --> 00:10:55.960
My intentions?

00:10:55.960 --> 00:10:58.920
If you wanted us to reset immediately,

00:10:59.260 --> 00:11:05.310
then there was no need to have us meet Sera
or give us detailed information regarding her ability.

00:11:06.560 --> 00:11:09.600
You're going to reset once you're satisfied, huh?

00:11:09.600 --> 00:11:11.190
Yes, that's right.

00:11:11.600 --> 00:11:13.310
Then it's fine.

00:11:13.310 --> 00:11:16.570
Hold on. I have a favor to ask.

00:11:16.570 --> 00:11:17.360
What is it?

00:11:19.280 --> 00:11:23.870
Please give me Sera's middle school
classmate's contact information.

00:11:29.080 --> 00:11:30.410
Well...

00:11:30.410 --> 00:11:32.670
I guess they've passed so far.

00:11:37.460 --> 00:11:39.090
Sorry if I'm a bother.

00:11:39.300 --> 00:11:41.220
I don't feel like you're being a nuisance.

00:11:41.430 --> 00:11:44.350
You and Asai are sort of strange.

00:11:44.930 --> 00:11:47.600
In what way are we strange?

00:11:47.810 --> 00:11:51.230
I feel like you two aren't normal.
Your relationship is weird.

00:11:51.560 --> 00:11:53.400
What do you mean by "relationship"?

00:11:53.400 --> 00:11:55.560
We're classmates, right?

00:11:55.560 --> 00:11:58.480
It doesn't seem right to speak politely.

00:11:58.480 --> 00:12:00.610
Is it better to speak casually?

00:12:00.900 --> 00:12:03.240
Well, I guess it'd feel more comfortable.

00:12:03.240 --> 00:12:04.700
Fine, let's do it.

00:12:04.700 --> 00:12:05.200
Huh?

00:12:05.530 --> 00:12:08.120
I won't get hung up on how I talk.

00:12:08.120 --> 00:12:09.200
Does that sound okay?

00:12:09.410 --> 00:12:12.620
It's weird. Why are you talking like that?

00:12:12.620 --> 00:12:14.630
I tried to imitate Kei.

00:12:14.630 --> 00:12:16.460
He speaks like this.

00:12:16.460 --> 00:12:18.380
It's fine to speak politely!

00:12:18.380 --> 00:12:20.710
That seems unnatural... and a little scary.

00:12:20.710 --> 00:12:22.130
Is that so?

00:12:22.130 --> 00:12:24.720
You really aren't normal.

00:12:24.720 --> 00:12:28.890
You're weird, but in a good way.
It makes you seem sort of special.

00:12:28.890 --> 00:12:32.770
"Weird" can be used to describe
something uncommon.

00:12:32.770 --> 00:12:35.310
I think uncommon things are special.

00:12:35.310 --> 00:12:36.610
That's not what I meant!

00:12:36.610 --> 00:12:40.900
I probably used to be weird myself,
but I wasn't special at all.

00:12:40.900 --> 00:12:42.990
I don't understand.

00:12:42.990 --> 00:12:47.370
You know, when I was in middle school,
I was always called by a weird nickname.

00:12:47.370 --> 00:12:51.250
But that nickname wasn't special in the slightest.

00:12:51.250 --> 00:12:53.620
I wanted to ditch that name as quickly as possible.

00:12:54.000 --> 00:12:55.790
Why did you want to ditch it?

00:12:57.670 --> 00:12:59.800
Because it's something I didn't need.

00:13:08.050 --> 00:13:10.430
I'm pretty sure of it.

00:13:12.770 --> 00:13:14.270
Morning, Kei.

00:13:15.270 --> 00:13:16.020
Morning.

00:13:16.230 --> 00:13:18.270
Did you get to know Sera better?

00:13:18.270 --> 00:13:20.230
Probably. In our own way.

00:13:27.160 --> 00:13:28.620
Did you change the way you speak?

00:13:28.820 --> 00:13:29.580
Yeah.

00:13:29.580 --> 00:13:33.700
Yesterday, Sera said it was weird for me
to speak politely since we're classmates.

00:13:33.700 --> 00:13:35.120
Oh, I see.

00:13:35.120 --> 00:13:37.330
Asai, you're okay with this?

00:13:37.620 --> 00:13:39.710
I think it suits her well.

00:13:39.710 --> 00:13:43.420
Thanks. I tried to copy the way you speak.

00:13:43.420 --> 00:13:46.470
But Sera said it was unnatural and scary.

00:13:46.720 --> 00:13:48.930
I don't think it's scary.

00:13:48.930 --> 00:13:50.390
It's just who I am.

00:13:50.720 --> 00:13:54.430
If you compare this to the way I normally speak,
which do you think is better for me?

00:13:55.770 --> 00:14:00.020
There are upsides to both, but I guess the
way you normally speak is more natural.

00:14:00.480 --> 00:14:03.150
I see. I'll speak as I always do, then.

00:14:03.150 --> 00:14:07.780
Shouldn't you guys hurry?
Our homeroom class is about to start.

00:14:07.780 --> 00:14:09.990
Not at all. It's totally fine.

00:14:09.990 --> 00:14:11.030
How so?

00:14:11.030 --> 00:14:13.740
We decided to skip school today.

00:14:14.040 --> 00:14:14.870
Wha—

00:14:18.750 --> 00:14:19.960
Is this okay?

00:14:19.960 --> 00:14:21.380
What do you mean?

00:14:21.380 --> 00:14:22.710
Being absent from school.

00:14:22.880 --> 00:14:26.050
The day after the entrance
ceremony isn't a big deal.

00:14:26.050 --> 00:14:27.720
You're okay with this, Misora?

00:14:27.720 --> 00:14:28.680
Yes.

00:14:28.680 --> 00:14:29.550
Why?!

00:14:29.800 --> 00:14:31.260
Because Kei decided it.

00:14:31.260 --> 00:14:33.180
Can you really call that a reason?

00:14:33.180 --> 00:14:33.930
Of course.

00:14:35.560 --> 00:14:36.930
Sorry.

00:14:36.930 --> 00:14:42.360
I'll try to get out of here on my own,
so you and Asai should go to school.

00:14:42.650 --> 00:14:44.820
Why do you care so much about school?

00:14:45.360 --> 00:14:47.440
I mean, you skipped the entrance ceremony.

00:14:47.440 --> 00:14:49.570
That's different!

00:14:49.570 --> 00:14:51.910
I needed to do that.

00:14:51.910 --> 00:14:53.870
What do you mean?

00:14:56.410 --> 00:15:01.420
They say that there is something pure within
the heart of a child who loves pure things.

00:15:01.790 --> 00:15:03.000
Something pure?

00:15:03.590 --> 00:15:04.670
Yeah.

00:15:06.670 --> 00:15:10.380
That's what my homeroom teacher said
in my third year of elementary school.

00:15:12.720 --> 00:15:13.720
Sera?

00:15:13.720 --> 00:15:14.350
Huh?

00:15:14.760 --> 00:15:16.270
You're still here?

00:15:16.270 --> 00:15:18.430
I'll be going home in a bit.

00:15:19.520 --> 00:15:21.350
Thank you for doing that.

00:15:22.810 --> 00:15:23.980
It's nothing.

00:15:24.730 --> 00:15:26.940
I just like pure water better.

00:15:27.780 --> 00:15:31.860
You have something very pure within your heart.

00:15:31.860 --> 00:15:33.070
Something pure?

00:15:33.370 --> 00:15:34.490
Yes.

00:15:34.490 --> 00:15:38.580
There is something pure within the heart
of a child who loves pure things.

00:15:39.450 --> 00:15:40.870
Close your eyes.

00:15:40.870 --> 00:15:44.210
Think of what you deem the purest.

00:15:44.960 --> 00:15:48.210
That is your purity.

00:15:48.210 --> 00:15:51.880
A very pure object that exists
only within your heart.

00:15:53.590 --> 00:15:58.220
I'm sure what you thought
of doesn't exist in this world.

00:15:58.810 --> 00:16:03.850
Still, there are plenty of things in
this world that are as pure as that.

00:16:03.850 --> 00:16:05.980
Where are they?

00:16:06.190 --> 00:16:08.190
They're everywhere!

00:16:08.190 --> 00:16:09.740
Tucked away in the blue skies,

00:16:10.400 --> 00:16:12.280
in the sound of the wind,

00:16:12.280 --> 00:16:14.570
and even in the words you say.

00:16:16.120 --> 00:16:18.410
As long as you have purity within your heart,

00:16:18.410 --> 00:16:21.830
you'll be able to find things
that are just as pure anywhere.

00:16:21.830 --> 00:16:23.250
I don't have anything like that.

00:16:23.620 --> 00:16:25.960
You do. I'm sure you do.

00:16:26.460 --> 00:16:32.380
Try comparing something you've seen or
thought of with the pure thing within your heart.

00:16:32.880 --> 00:16:36.550
Once you do that, you'll be able
to find nothing but pure things.

00:16:36.550 --> 00:16:37.800
Really?

00:16:37.800 --> 00:16:40.560
